{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"durable-qualified-pelican","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/drift_floor.py:126` (`drift_floor_candidate`) computes the\ndrift-refresh eligibility `code_drifted` reason as:\n\n```python\nsigned_sha = signing.verified_at_sha_from_manifest(manifest)   # the GATE-REF sha at review time\ncurrent_sha = signing.head_sha(_config.repo_root(repo_root))    # git rev-parse HEAD of the working tree\nreasons[\"code_drifted\"] = bool(signed_sha) and bool(current_sha) and current_sha != \"unknown\" and signed_sha != current_sha\n```\n\nThis is the SAME defect class as bug `1137-8215-ec04-4ca0` (seaworthy-revengeful-blobfish): it\ncompares the signed **gate-ref** sha (`verified_at_sha`) against `git rev-parse HEAD` of whatever\nworking tree the evaluator sits in. Its own comment states it \"mirrors compute_validity's unscoped\nwhole-HEAD 'stale-head' trigger anchor **exactly**\" — and 1137's fix corrected compute_validity's\nunscoped trigger to resolve the CURRENT gate ref (via `resolve_ref(default_ref, working, fetch=False)`,\n`source=local`/legacy tolerant, fail-closed on unresolvable). This site was NOT updated, so it now\nDIVERGES from the invariant its comment asserts.\n\n## Impact (why this is P3, not P2)\nUnlike 1137 this does NOT block claims. `drift_floor_candidate` is the drift-refresh REUSE floor: a\nspurious `code_drifted=True` only DENIES cheap-refresh eligibility, forcing a (safe but wasteful)\nFULL re-review, and makes `_drifted_paths(signed_sha, current_sha)` diff the gate-ref sha against a\nFOREIGN commit (bogus drifted-file lists). Conservative/wasteful, not incorrect-blocking.\n\n## Non-trivial subtlety (DO NOT fix blind)\ndrift_floor's failure semantics DIFFER from attest.py's: `code_drifted` guards `current_sha != \"unknown\"`,\nso an UNRESOLVABLE current sha reads as NOT drifted → **fail-OPEN** (would reuse a possibly-stale review).\nattest.py fails CLOSED on the same condition. A correct fix must resolve the current gate-ref sha AND\nhandle resolution failure so it does not introduce a fail-open drift-refresh reuse. This needs its own\nRED->GREEN test (attested manifest, origin/main unmoved, foreign working-tree HEAD -> code_drifted must\nbe False/eligible; gate ref moved -> code_drifted True; gate ref unresolvable -> conservative not-eligible).\n\n## Suggested approach\nMirror 1137's attest.py fix: resolve `resolve_ref(gate_source.default_ref(working), working, fetch=False)`\nfor attested manifests (source=local / no-verified_at_sha keep head_sha), and map a SnapshotError to a\nconservative not-eligible outcome (NOT eligible), preserving drift_floor's fail-safe direction. Consider a\nshared helper with attest.py's `_unscoped_head_drift` so the documented mirror invariant holds by construction.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `drift_floor_candidate` resolves the CURRENT gate ref (not working-tree HEAD) for attested manifests.\n- [ ] source=local and no-verified_at_sha manifests keep the working-tree basis (unchanged).\n- [ ] Gate-ref resolution failure yields a CONSERVATIVE not-eligible outcome (no fail-open reuse).\n- [ ] RED->GREEN test proves the foreign-working-tree false-drift is gone and moved/unresolvable ref semantics preserved.\n- [ ] Mirror invariant with compute_validity's unscoped trigger restored (ideally a shared helper).","id":"3409-9824-6d4e-469f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"drift_floor_candidate reads working-tree HEAD, not the gate ref, for attested code-drift eligibility (1137 sibling)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788048239176694001,"uuid":"d78dddf9-bb8c-4b48-9f4f-d89f445069a2"}